# Version ceilings for the image build.

# nvidia-drivers 610.x added an unconditional "sys-devel/gcc:*" to RDEPEND — the open kernel
# modules are rebuilt on the running system, so the driver expects a toolchain to be present.
# That would put a full compiler in the image and break plan/06's toolchain-free guarantee
# (and it could not work anyway on a read-only /usr). 595.x is the newest branch without that
# dependency; it still ships the open GSP modules, prebuilt here against gentoo-kernel-bin.
# Revisit if upstream drops the runtime-toolchain requirement — or move to nouveau if it never does.
>=x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers-610

# ---- the GNOME ban (plan/09) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Belt-and-braces. config/portage/expected-packages.txt remains the primary gate, but a mask
# fails the build AT DEPENDENCY RESOLUTION and names the package that pulled the offender,
# which is far easier to act on than a 500-line diff at stage 50.
#
# mirror_target_pkg_config() (scripts/lib/common.sh) copies this file onto the BUILDER's "/"
# as well, so every entry applies to both roots. That is fine now that @buildhost is empty and
# the builder's own emerge list contains no GNOME desktop package — but it is exactly why this
# list must stay curated rather than becoming "gnome-base/*". gnome-base/librsvg is emerged on
# the builder for rsvg-convert (builder/Dockerfile), and a category wildcard would kill it.
gnome-base/gnome-shell
gnome-base/gnome-session
gnome-base/gnome-settings-daemon
gnome-base/gnome-control-center
gnome-base/gnome-keyring
gnome-base/nautilus
gnome-base/gdm
gnome-base/gvfs
gnome-base/gnome-desktop
gnome-base/libgtop
# Covers gnome-software, gnome-system-monitor, evolution-data-server, gnome-color-manager,
# nm-applet, polkit-gnome and tecla in one line.
gnome-extra/*
gui-apps/gnome-console
gui-libs/libadwaita
gui-libs/vte
dev-libs/gjs
x11-wm/mutter
x11-themes/gnome-backgrounds
sys-apps/xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
# xdg-desktop-portal-kde implements the full interface set (FileChooser, Settings, Screenshot,
# ScreenCast, Print, Inhibit, Account, GlobalShortcuts), so the GTK *backend* has no job. The
# GTK *theming* bridge is a separate thing and stays.
sys-apps/xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
# GNOME's file indexer. kde-frameworks/baloo replaces it, so this bans a DUPLICATE indexer,
# not indexing — see the baloo block in package.use/image and /etc/xdg/baloofilerc.
app-misc/localsearch
app-misc/tinysparql
app-arch/gnome-autoar
x11-misc/xdg-user-dirs-gtk
media-libs/libcanberra-gtk3
sci-geosciences/geocode-glib
# The GNOME printer UI. kde-plasma/print-manager talks to CUPS directly and nothing in the
# Plasma set asks for this, so the mask still catches the old printer-panel cascade coming
# back — while leaving net-fs/samba, which IS wanted (kio-extras[samba], for smb:// in
# Dolphin), deliberately unmasked.
app-admin/system-config-printer
# Browser engines: nothing native renders HTML here (plan/03). Structural, not flag-dependent
# — USE=-webengine is the flag half of the same guard.
net-libs/webkit-gtk
dev-qt/qtwebengine

